{
	"id": "running-effects",
	"text": "So now that we've defined our effect, how do we get our hands on its juicy result? Remember, because effects are lazy, we have to explicitly run them. For simple, synchronous effects, we can use Effect.runSync. This runs the effect immediately and returns the value. However, in real applications, Effects probably involve async work. We'll mostly use Effect.runPromise, running our effect as a Promise, which, mind you, is not lazy, but a handle on a running computation.",
	"code": "import { Effect } from \"effect\"\n\nconst magicWord = Effect.succeed(\"pismire\")",
